{
    "id": "7ef8e64a-08b6-46d8-8b67-c8dfa7743ccc",
    "indications": "CREXONT is indicated for the treatment of Parkinson's disease, post-encephalitic parkinsonism, and parkinsonism that may follow carbon monoxide intoxication or manganese intoxication in adults.",
    "contraindications": "Evaluate vitamin B6 levels prior to starting treatment with carbidopa/levodopa therapies. ( 2.1 ) Levodopa-naïve patients: Starting dose is 35 mg carbidopa / 140 mg levodopa taken orally twice daily for the first 3 days; on the fourth day of treatment, dosage may be increased gradually as needed. ( 2.2 ) Patients converting from immediate-release carbidopa/levodopa: See Table 1 for instructions; dosages are not substitutable on a 1:1 basis. ( 2.3 ) The maximum recommended daily dosage of CREXONT is 525 mg carbidopa / 2100 mg levodopa. ( 2.2 , 2.3 ) CREXONT may be taken with or without food; do not chew, divide, or crush. ( 2.5 , 12.3 ) CREXONT should not be taken with alcohol. ( 2.5 , 12.3 )",
    "adverseReactions": "CREXONT is contraindicated in patients currently taking a nonselective monoamine oxidase (MAO) inhibitor or have recently (within 2 weeks) taken a nonselective MAO inhibitor. Hypertension can occur if these drugs are used concurrently [see Drug Interactions (7.1)].",
